Static Variables:

The static keyword in C is used to declare static variables. When a variable is declared static, it has a lifetime that extends for the entire duration of the program. This means that the variable is initialized once and retains its value between function calls. Static variables can be declared inside a function (local static variables) or outside of any function (global static variables).

Local Static Variables:

